# The SNMP agent as a management API: the VRFs it runs in. MAXSIZE is always printed and keeps one
# row when the agent runs nowhere. With no community and no user, cEOS 4.36 still prints "SNMP
# agent enabled in VRFs: default", then "SNMP agent disabled: ..." at the end
# (testdata/lab/sw1nosnmp_show_snmp.raw): that line clears what was captured, so the recipe says
# enabled: no and lists no VRF.
Value VRFS (.+?)
Value MAXSIZE (\d+)
Value DISABLED (\S.*?)

Start
  ^SNMP agent disabled: -> Continue.Clear
  ^SNMP agent disabled:\s+${DISABLED}\s*$$
  ^SNMP agent enabled in VRFs:\s+${VRFS}\s*$$
  ^Transmit message maximum size:\s+${MAXSIZE}\s*$$
